/// Module 11. The collection lifecycle, answering the source's Open Questions
/// 8, 9 and 10 explicitly.
///
/// `CREATED → SYNCED → POSTED → REVERSED` is the source's own lifecycle. Only
/// `POSTED` and `REVERSED` are authoritative money: an offline record is
/// non-authoritative until the server posts it (Rule 39).
///
/// `FAILED` exists because Scenario 48 requires a failed receipt-sequence
/// attempt to be "retained for controlled retry". It is never a state the
/// posting transaction commits — a throw rolls that transaction back — so it is
/// written by the outer catch in a separate transaction, exactly as
/// `DISBURSEMENT_LEDGER_FAILED` is audited outside the rolled-back work.
enum CollectionStatus {
  CREATED
  SYNCED
  POSTED
  REVERSED
  FAILED

  @@map("collection_status")
}

